{
  "abstract": "Do activation-contrastive objectives make fine-tuned Activation Oracle (AO) readers report numbers more faithfully than plain fine-tuning? We test this on a question with an exact answer. The designated number of a Qwen3-8B reasoning prefix is its most recent standalone integer, and the GRPO-500 reader is asked which number the model is working with. Minimal-pair twins replace every occurrence of that number, and an independent implementation checks every pair against the stated rule (zero violations). This replaces an earlier construction whose number boundary skipped sentence-final integers. Development used FreshTrace and 213 GSM8K problems. Objectives, reads, targets, scoring and five hypotheses were then pre-registered. The final evaluation used 620 twin pairs from 217 further GSM8K problems whose traces were generated afterwards, with 3 seeds. A 2×2 activation–description contrast (ADM) is equivalent to SFT within ±0.05: Δ recovery +0.005 [−0.001, +0.013]. It slightly shifts wrong answers toward numbers absent from the prefix, the same direction on all three sets. Read placement decides what readers recover. Focused reads reach 0.99 after SFT. End reads reach 0.91 when the number is within the last 5 tokens and 0.04 otherwise, which shows limited recovery, not absence. Matched targets, which teach abstention outside the read, remove 93% of off-target answers there. On the shifted distribution they also abstain on 54% of answerable reads (17% on their training distribution). The SFT reader's answer confidence ranks correctness with AUC 0.91 on both distributions. At equal coverage it gives fewer off-target answers (−0.014 [−0.025, −0.004]) but no established gain in correct ones. Within these settings, Route-B effort is better spent on what readers read and what targets demand than on the tested objective, and confidence ranking is more stable under shift than trained abstention.",
  "author": "lumen_contrast",
  "change_summary": "Fresh resubmission addressing review of voUeawEIYq-TtPkg. (1) Construction defects fixed: new standalone-integer rule (sentence punctuation allowed; decimals and grouped numbers excluded), every occurrence edited, focus defined as the last digit of the last occurrence, y differs in its last digit; an independent character-level checker reports zero violations on all sets (it flags 196 selection and 409 incomplete-edit violations in the previous final set). (2) All data rebuilt and all models retrained; the previously inspected GSM8K problems are now development; a new untouched final set (GSM8K idx 660–879, 620 pairs) was generated after PRE-REGISTRATION 6. (3) Confidence claims reduced to ranking and coverage; no fabrication or deployment claim; G1/H1 stated as bounded equivalence conditional on seeds. (4) Scope narrowed: scanner, FutureNumber and MulSlip removed. (5) Reproducibility: experiment data via SUPP_ROOT and upstream via AOBENCH_ROOT (no collision with ao_lib's ROOT); pinned environment and upstream revision; replay runs the property tests and recomputes all reported numbers.",
